From: CarPlay C0 lane (2026-11-21)
Subject: 0511 sweet_nub: the mode value selects the personality (no second boot argument)

0510 added sweet_nub_ibridge as a second boot argument. That does not fit: the assembled cmdline
of the S3 image is already 603 of the 607 usable bytes, and mkpayload refuses the image once the
line grows ("boot arguments exceed 607 bytes") -- measured while building the iBridge image.

So the personality rides on the existing integer: sweet_nub=1 keeps the default ncmBringup,
sweet_nub=2 selects iBridgeBringup (AppleUSBMux + AppleUSBNCMControl + AppleUSBNCMData). Same one
character, no length change, no extra knob. The registration line now prints the personality it
actually published instead of a hardcoded name, and the log checker accepts either value.

--- a/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
@@ -208,19 +208,16 @@
 
 	/* prepareDefaults overwrites ConfigurationType; set the matching value now and
 	 * publish, which is what starts personality matching (IOService.h:650). */
-	/* Personality selection: the four IOUSBDeviceFamily personalities differ only in the
-	 * InterfaceAssociation/Interfaces sets, so this is the one knob that decides whether the
-	 * host sees plain NCM (AppleUSBNCMControl/Data) or the CarPlay-capable iBridge set
-	 * (AppleUSBMux + NCM). Making it a boot argument turns a personality change from a CI
-	 * round + image rebuild into a single bootarg, which is exactly what an A/B needs. */
-	int ibridge = 0;
-	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweet_nub_ibridge", &ibridge, sizeof(ibridge));
-	const char *personality = ibridge ? "iBridgeBringup" : "ncmBringup";
+	/* 0511: the mode argument doubles as the personality selector -- sweet_nub=1 is the NCM
+	 * personality, sweet_nub=2 is iBridgeBringup (AppleUSBMux + NCM). A separate boot argument
+	 * would not fit: the assembled cmdline is already 603 of the 607 usable bytes, so growing it
+	 * by a second flag makes mkpayload refuse the image. One integer, one knob, no length risk. */
+	const char *personality = (run_start == 2) ? "iBridgeBringup" : "ncmBringup";
 	ctl->setProperty("ConfigurationType", personality);
-	printf("SWEET NUB: ConfigurationType=%s%s\n", personality,
-	    ibridge ? " (sweet_nub_ibridge=1)" : " (pass sweet_nub_ibridge=1 for iBridge)");
+	printf("SWEET NUB: ConfigurationType=%s (sweet_nub=%d%s)\n", personality, run_start,
+	    run_start == 2 ? "" : "; pass 2 for iBridge");
 	ctl->registerService();
-	printf("SWEET NUB: registered as ncmBringup; mux/configurator should now match\n");
+	printf("SWEET NUB: registered as %s; mux/configurator should now match\n", personality);
 }
 
 #endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET */
